  "image_name": "72f2995fd292990956ba9413dae2614d.png",
  "prompt_text": "The figure summarizes an open quantum system picture and how two kinds of environmental coupling affect a qubit-like state on the Bloch sphere. On the left, the “system” is embedded in an “environment,” with the interaction written in terms of dephasing and decay channels. The labels indicate dephasing through a coupling involving the \\(z\\)-component of the spin and decay through raising and lowering operators, showing that the environment changes the system Hamiltonian and density matrix.\n\nThe two spheres on the right illustrate the resulting dynamics using the expectation values \\(\\langle \\sigma_x\\rangle\\), \\(\\langle \\sigma_y\\rangle\\), and \\(\\langle \\sigma_z\\rangle\\). In the middle panel, many blue trajectories from different starting points bend upward and converge toward the north pole, while a highlighted red path does the same. This visually represents relaxation toward a preferred polarized state. In the right panel, the arrows are mostly horizontal, circling at fixed height, and the highlighted red path moves around a latitude rather than toward a pole. That pattern indicates loss of phase coherence without strong population transfer: the state keeps its \\(z\\)-projection but its transverse components are damped. Overall, the figure contrasts dissipation-driven relaxation with pure dephasing.",
